<section class='content page-content colophon'>
  <h1>colophon</h1>

  <p>
    This is a small house on the internet. It is intentionally personal, a
    little strange, and built to feel more like a corner of the web than a
    portfolio.
  </p>

  <h2>why it looks like this</h2>

  <p>
    I like old web pages, terminal interfaces, tiny badges, webrings, monospace
    text, and websites that feel made by a person. The chrome is part of the
    personality, but the content is the point.
  </p>

  <h2>how it is built</h2>

  <p>
    11ty turns Markdown and Nunjucks templates into static HTML. CSS and vanilla
    JavaScript provide the interface. There is no client framework running the
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>the rule</h2>

  <p>Keep it small. Keep it weird. Make the internet feel human.</p>

  <p class='muted'>amdkits.me · source-controlled · hand assembled</p>
</section>
